menu "CrowPanel Advanced P4 board"

    config BOARD_CROWPANEL_P4_ES8311
        bool
        help
            The board may carry an ES8311 codec on its sound lines (the 10.1in V1.2's
            schematic draws one): at start it is looked for at I2C0 0x18 and, where it
            answers, clocked from GPIO24 and set up. Where none answers the sound is plain
            I2S, as on the 7in, and GPIO24 is let go. Selected by the board component
            (board_crowpanel_10/Kconfig), never by hand.

    config BOARD_FLICKER_GUARD
        bool "Turn the backlight off when the display refresh stalls"
        default y
        help
            Photosensitivity safety. The display refresh is timed every frame; at the first
            late frame the backlight goes off, and it comes back only after the refresh has
            been steady for BOARD_FLICKER_GUARD_HOLD_S seconds. Keeps a stalling display from
            ever showing as a flashing screen.

    config BOARD_FLICKER_GUARD_HOLD_S
        int "Seconds of steady refresh before the backlight comes back"
        depends on BOARD_FLICKER_GUARD
        range 2 600
        default 10

    config BOARD_FRAME_CAPTURE
        bool "Let the app copy the screen (remote viewing and screenshots)"
        default y
        help
            Keeps track of which DSI frame buffer holds the last complete frame, so that
            board_dev_frame() can copy it for the Panel Manager's remote keypad and the
            developer screenshot (docs/features/30, /31). Costs one LVGL event per flush.

    config BOARD_BACKLIGHT_FORCE_OFF
        bool "Keep the backlight off (test builds)"
        default n
        help
            The display and UI run normally but the backlight never turns on. For testing
            display changes without anyone looking at the screen (console: "display").

    config BOARD_DISPLAY_DIAG
        bool "Display self-check (investigation builds)"
        default n
        help
            Compares every flush with the frame buffer and marks pixels no object paints
            (docs/bugs/B023); logs the chip temperature with the counts. Slows each redraw by
            a few milliseconds: for investigation builds only. Console: "dispdiag".

endmenu
